
 ##Methods-
         -A block of code that does a specific work or task.
         -method is name set of instructions that we can call whenever needed.
         -Abstraction not possible without method.
         -Polymorphism not possible without method.

     Advantages-
        -code become reusable.
        -code become modular.
        -Easy to read.
        -Easy to test.
        -Easy to maintain.

Types of methods-
        1.predefined method
                    -already available methods
                    -eg. System.out.println();
                    -eg. main method

        2.build-in method(User defined method)
                    -method created by programmer.
                    -eg. void additionOfNumbers();

             * types-
                    1.method with return type
                    2.method without return type
                    3.method with parameters
                    4.method without parameters
                    5.static method
#static keyword -
            -when we put static in front of something(variables, methods, classes) it
                means this belongs to the class not to an object.
            -it will have only one copy in a memory(only one copy means
                that member exists in a memory regardless of how many objects of the
                class we create.)


#Instance method -
            -An every method declared without static keyword is called instance method.
